## Summary

Ported all **5 hooks** from `web/src/api/hooks/useChat.ts` to a UI-free KMP shared-core state holder, verified against `devtools.ts`, `router.go`, and `chatbot/dtos.go`.

**Reads (2):** `chatSessions()` ΓåÆ `GET /chatbot/sessions`; `chatHistory(id)` ΓåÆ `GET /chatbot/history?session_id=` (with the web `enabled: !!sessionId` gate). Both exposed as shared cache-then-network `StateFlow<Resource<T>>`.

**Mutations (3):** `renameChatSession` (PATCH, id percent-encoded, body `{title}`), `deleteChatSession` (DELETE 204), `sendChatMessage` (POST, drops `session_id` when null). Rename/delete optimistically patch the cached session list (the `setQueryData` analogue) and the store refreshes the sessions feed (`invalidateQueries` analogue); delete also evicts the session's history key (`removeQueries` analogue). Send has no cache interaction.

